  (41819, 157, 'that I loved -', 88.806, 89.966, NULL),
  (41820, 157, 'to my crack dealer
for four 20-dollar rocks.', 89.966, 95.397, NULL),
  (41821, 157, 'That memory is so painful that,', 97.294, 99.949, NULL),
  (41822, 157, 'actually, this is the first time
I''ve ever shared it publicly.', 100.370, 103.558, NULL),
  (41823, 157, 'I came as close to giving up on life
as one can without jumping off,', 106.110, 111.996, NULL),
  (41824, 157, 'but something extraordinary happened
to me the second time I went to prison.', 112.943, 117.011, NULL),
  (41825, 157, 'About two months into my sentence,', 118.532, 121.218, NULL),
  (41826, 157, 'I got a letter from my ex-wife', 121.218, 123.512, NULL),
  (41827, 157, 'telling me that my mother,', 124.707, 127.733, NULL),
  (41828, 157, 'the person I profess
to love and care about', 128.253, 130.801, NULL),
  (41829, 157, 'more than anyone in the world,', 130.801, 132.681, NULL),
  (41830, 157, 'had had a heart attack', 132.681, 134.618, NULL),
  (41831, 157, 'and was likely going to die.', 136.449, 138.886, NULL),
  (41832, 157, 'This wasn''t my biological mother,', 139.998, 142.897, NULL),
  (41833, 157, 'who had abandoned me
shortly after I was born,', 142.897, 146.090, NULL),
  (41834, 157, 'but the real mother who had raised me
as her own for all of my life.', 146.090, 151.991, NULL),
  (41835, 157, 'I was forced to look at', 155.061, 158.864, NULL),
  (41836, 157, 'what kind of person I had become,', 158.864, 162.147, NULL),
  (41837, 157, 'and the person I had become
was not easy to look at.', 163.709, 168.369, NULL),
  (41838, 157, 'Because I had become the son', 169.433, 171.995, NULL),
  (41839, 157, 'who would not be there
to comfort his 77-year-old mother,', 171.995, 177.643, NULL),
  (41840, 157, 'laying all alone
in a stark hospital room,', 178.203, 182.246, NULL),
  (41841, 157, 'when she needed him the most,', 182.871, 184.949, NULL),
  (41842, 157, 'because of my selfish need
to escape my realities', 185.899, 190.271, NULL),
  (41843, 157, 'by getting high.', 193.502, 194.806, NULL),
  (41844, 157, 'In a moment of brutal honesty,', 197.099, 199.997, NULL),
  (41845, 157, 'I had to admit I had been living a lie.', 200.507, 204.319, NULL),
  (41846, 157, 'I was not the loving son,
or the faithful partner,', 206.135, 211.802, NULL),
  (41847, 157, 'or the supportive father,
or the good citizen', 211.802, 215.715, NULL),
  (41848, 157, 'that I had been telling everyone
including myself, for years.', 216.615, 220.265, NULL),
  (41849, 157, 'It was then that I decided', 222.454, 224.456, NULL),
  (41850, 157, 'that I needed to try to change my life', 224.456, 228.247, NULL),
  (41851, 157, 'into something that I and my mother,', 230.212, 235.255, NULL),
  (41852, 157, 'wherever she might be,', 236.585, 238.283, NULL),
  (41853, 157, 'could be proud of.', 238.793, 240.263, NULL),
  (41854, 157, 'And a tiny seed of change
was planted deep inside me.', 242.953, 247.852, NULL),
  (41855, 157, 'So after my release from prison,', 250.079, 252.137, NULL),
  (41856, 157, 'I decided I would go back to school,', 252.137, 253.930, NULL),
  (41857, 157, 'because I figured what better place', 255.728, 258.200, NULL),
  (41858, 157, 'can a middle-aged,
240-pound, black, ex-convict go', 259.440, 265.250, NULL),
  (41859, 157, '(Laughter)', 265.250, 267.222, NULL),
  (41860, 157, 'to blend in', 267.222, 268.561, NULL),
  (41861, 157, '(Laughter)', 268.561, 271.561, NULL),
  (41862, 157, 'than a white-bred community college', 272.634, 274.973, NULL),
  (41863, 157, 'with a whole bunch
of 20-something coeds.', 274.973, 277.527, NULL),
  (41864, 157, '(Laughter)', 277.527, 279.249, NULL),
  (41865, 157, 'But I was fortunate', 281.435, 284.705, NULL),
  (41866, 157, 'because at the local
junior college where I landed,', 284.705, 288.244, NULL),
  (41867, 157, 'I ran into two instructors
that changed my life.', 288.244, 292.101, NULL),
  (41868, 157, 'It was my interactions
with these instructors', 293.998, 296.432, NULL),
  (41869, 157, 'that helped me to regain the self-worth
and purpose and meaning and confidence', 296.432, 303.072, NULL),
  (41870, 157, 'that my drug use and drug-related
lifestyle had stolen from me.', 303.072, 308.333, NULL),
  (41871, 157, 'I''ll never forget the moment', 309.704, 313.503, NULL),
  (41872, 157, 'that I realized', 314.423, 316.261, NULL),
  (41873, 157, 'that I understood', 317.271, 318.713, NULL),
  (41874, 157, 'that I could create my own miracle.', 319.203, 322.589, NULL),
  (41875, 157, 'It all started when I went up to one
of Professor Sina''s office hours,', 324.524, 331.201, NULL),
  (41876, 157, 'fishing for some special praise', 332.234, 335.735, NULL),
  (41877, 157, 'because that had become
my new drug of choice.', 335.735, 338.955, NULL),
  (41878, 157, 'She listened to me, described
some super cool thing I had just done,', 340.745, 346.310, NULL),
  (41879, 157, 'and with no pomp and circumstance,', 348.369, 350.473, NULL),
  (41880, 157, 'she looked at me and said,', 350.473, 353.051, NULL),
  (41881, 157, '''''Isn''t it amazing, B.J.,', 354.384, 356.613, NULL),
  (41882, 157, 'what a person can do
when they start believing in themselves.''''', 356.613, 360.411, NULL),
  (41883, 157, 'And then, as if nothing special
had happened,', 363.126, 365.476, NULL),
  (41884, 157, 'she turned back to her desk
at what she was doing.', 365.476, 368.104, NULL),
  (41885, 157, 'While I walked away from that office hour,', 371.584, 374.039, NULL),
  (41886, 157, 'dazed and confused,
and wondering what had happened,', 374.039, 378.226, NULL),
  (41887, 157, 'I was also a little pissed
because she hadn''t fed my new habit.', 379.321, 384.778, NULL),
  (41888, 157, 'But I was forced to think about
what had happened', 387.353, 392.716, NULL),
  (41889, 157, 'and what did it mean.', 392.716, 394.519, NULL),
  (41890, 157, 'And importantly,', 396.993, 398.857, NULL),
  (41891, 157, 'that seed of change
that was deep inside me', 398.857, 402.180, NULL),
  (41892, 157, 'started to stir.', 402.180, 404.031, NULL),
  (41893, 157, 'A couple months later,', 406.336, 407.646, NULL),
  (41894, 157, 'while taking a test,', 408.716, 410.256, NULL),
  (41895, 157, 'Professor Miller', 410.646, 412.130, NULL),
  (41896, 157, 'walked by my desk and dropped off
an application that I later discovered', 413.261, 418.607, NULL),
  (41897, 157, 'was to the masters of counseling program
at Sacramento State University.', 419.053, 424.305, NULL),
  (41898, 157, 'So after the test,
I hurried up to his office hour and ...', 425.902, 428.741, NULL),
  (41899, 157, 'ran into his office', 430.363, 431.558, NULL),
  (41900, 157, 'and held up the application
and very obtusely said,', 431.558, 434.291, NULL),
  (41901, 157, '''''What''s this?''''', 434.710, 435.918, NULL),
  (41902, 157, 'And without hesitation, he responded,', 438.997, 441.267, NULL),
  (41903, 157, '''''I am quite confident
in your ability to read,', 441.267, 443.474, NULL),
  (41904, 157, 'so I''m sure you can
figure that out on your own.''''', 443.474, 445.998, NULL),
  (41905, 157, '(Laughter)', 445.998, 448.055, NULL),
  (41906, 157, 'So I brilliantly followed that up
with an equally obtuse question.', 450.955, 455.549, NULL),
  (41907, 157, 'I said, ''''So do you think I can do this?''''', 456.603, 460.269, NULL),
  (41908, 157, 'And with patience but no special fanfare,', 462.213, 467.261, NULL),
  (41909, 157, 'he looked at me and said,', 467.261, 469.585, NULL),
  (41910, 157, '''''Of course.''''', 471.598, 472.852, NULL),
  (41911, 157, '''''Of course.''''', 475.265, 476.265, NULL),
  (41912, 157, 'And then, he too turned back
around to his desk,', 477.474, 481.150, NULL),
  (41913, 157, 'signaling that we were done.', 481.150, 483.699, NULL),
  (41914, 157, '(Laughter)', 483.699, 485.773, NULL),
  (41915, 157, 'And again, I stumbled away
from an office hour, dazed and confused.', 485.783, 491.316, NULL),
  (41916, 157, 'But this time,', 493.275, 494.775, NULL),
  (41917, 157, 'the seeds of believing in myself', 497.179, 502.297, NULL),
  (41918, 157, 'that had been planted
in my garden of self-doubt', 503.218, 506.857, NULL),
  (41919, 157, 'took root', 508.027, 509.212, NULL),
  (41920, 157, 'and started to grow.', 510.065, 511.541, NULL),
  (41921, 157, 'In a moment, I realized', 515.481, 518.279, NULL),
  (41922, 157, 'that the only person left
to believe in me,', 519.000, 523.238, NULL),
  (41923, 157, 'that needed to believe in me,', 524.155, 526.559, NULL),
  (41924, 157, 'was me.', 527.234, 528.370, NULL),
  (41925, 157, 'As my tears started to well up in my eyes,', 532.930, 538.363, NULL),
  (41926, 157, 'for the first time
since I had left prison,', 540.217, 543.863, NULL),
  (41927, 157, 'I felt free.', 544.889, 545.968, NULL),
  (41928, 157, 'After three years,', 548.471, 550.611, NULL),
  (41929, 157, 'I finally felt free of the mental
and emotional shackles', 550.611, 557.245, NULL),
  (41930, 157, 'caused by the shame and the pain', 557.245, 559.819, NULL),
  (41931, 157, 'and the despair of my years of drug use.', 559.819, 566.453, NULL),
  (41932, 157, 'For years, I had been -
I and people like me -', 570.794, 575.496, NULL),
  (41933, 157, 'we had been told,', 576.086, 577.585, NULL),
  (41934, 157, '''''Once an addict, always an addict.''''', 578.136, 580.271, NULL),
  (41935, 157, '''''Once a criminal, always a criminal.''''', 580.271, 582.894, NULL),
  (41936, 157, '''''Once a loser, always a loser.''''', 582.894, 585.206, NULL),
  (41937, 157, 'But I realized that was only true
if you believed it.', 587.700, 593.502, NULL),
  (41938, 157, 'I have learned the hard way
how paralyzing self-doubt can be.', 596.842, 603.842, NULL),
  (41939, 157, 'It contributes to people
choosing misery over joy', 605.666, 609.916, NULL),
  (41940, 157, 'and emptiness over fulfillment', 610.301, 614.234, NULL),
  (41941, 157, 'and imprisonment over freedom -', 614.234, 619.563, NULL),
  (41942, 157, 'and unnecessarily so.', 620.667, 622.372, NULL),
  (41943, 157, 'In 2006,', 625.197, 627.297, NULL),
  (41944, 157, 'only seven years after I walked off
the yard at Corcoran State Prison,', 629.566, 634.014, NULL),
  (41945, 157, 'I walked across a stage,', 634.655, 636.315, NULL),
  (41946, 157, 'and I was conferred my doctorate
in clinical psychology.', 637.732, 642.549, NULL),
  (41947, 157, '(Applause)', 643.241, 646.221, NULL),
  (41948, 157, 'And sitting in the middle of the third row', 652.846, 658.239, NULL),
  (41949, 157, 'was a woman,', 659.119, 660.549, NULL),
  (41950, 157, 'who had spent countless, sleepless nights
worrying about her son.', 661.979, 667.264, NULL),
  (41951, 157, 'That woman was my then 85-year-old mother,', 668.748, 672.162, NULL),
  (41952, 157, 'who did not die while I was in prison,', 672.162, 674.868, NULL),
  (41953, 157, '(Applause)', 674.868, 677.872, NULL),
  (41954, 157, 'but lived to see me become the man
she always believed I could be.', 681.222, 687.258, NULL),
  (41955, 157, 'Prior to 1999,', 690.637, 692.426, NULL),
  (41956, 157, 'this was my life.', 693.714, 695.274, NULL),
  (41957, 157, 'without hope or purpose.', 696.277, 699.041, NULL),
  (41958, 157, 'Today,', 700.330, 701.433, NULL),
  (41959, 157, 'this is my life.', 703.016, 704.334, NULL),
  (41960, 157, 'Now, I want to say here
that I''m often frustrated', 707.603, 712.202, NULL),
  (41961, 157, 'when I hear people attribute
a person''s successful recovery', 712.202, 716.817, NULL),
  (41962, 157, 'or rehabilitation to a miracle,', 718.592, 722.560, NULL),
  (41963, 157, 'as if their hard work and perseverance
had nothing to do with it.', 723.351, 728.294, NULL),
  (41964, 157, 'I needed to say that', 730.586, 731.822, NULL),
  (41965, 157, 'because it was regaining
my belief in myself', 731.822, 735.505, NULL),
  (41966, 157, 'that gave me the power
to change the direction of my life.', 735.505, 740.373, NULL),
  (41967, 157, 'And it''s what allows me', 741.002, 743.843, NULL),
  (41968, 157, 'to now provide hope to others
facing similar challenges.', 743.843, 748.765, NULL),
  (41969, 157, 'Because I''m living proof,', 750.197, 753.906, NULL),
  (41970, 157, 'I''m living proof that a person''s past
does not have to define their future.', 755.398, 761.392, NULL),
  (41971, 157, 'Now,', 765.953, 766.953, NULL),
  (41972, 157, 'you don''t have to go to prison', 769.531, 771.436, NULL),
  (41973, 157, '(Laughter)', 772.539, 773.801, NULL),
  (41974, 157, 'to learn the lessons I have.', 775.359, 777.643, NULL),
  (41975, 157, 'In fact,', 778.659, 779.944, NULL),
  (41976, 157, 'I really wouldn''t recommend it.', 781.018, 783.217, NULL),
  (41977, 157, '(Laughter)', 783.217, 784.483, NULL),
  (41978, 157, 'But know this.', 786.888, 788.224, NULL),
  (41979, 157, 'We do have a choice', 791.075, 792.429, NULL),
  (41980, 157, 'whether we want to have our past define us', 792.429, 798.296, NULL),
  (41981, 157, 'or refine us.', 799.303, 801.541, NULL),
  (41982, 157, 'And as I tell the thousands of individuals', 803.343, 807.040, NULL),
  (41983, 157, 'struggling with addictions
and other painful life challenges', 807.865, 811.756, NULL),
  (41984, 157, 'that come through our clinic:', 811.756, 813.915, NULL),
  (41985, 157, 'You don''t have to wait for a miracle.', 815.978, 820.378, NULL),
  (41986, 157, 'You can create your own.', 821.192, 823.819, NULL),
  (41987, 157, 'Thank you.', 823.819, 825.019, NULL),
  (41988, 157, '(Applause)', 825.019, 828.011, NULL),
  (41989, 158, 'Most people wrestle with self-doubt
their entire lives', 0.000, 3.880, NULL),
  (41990, 158, 'and think it''s something
you just have to live with.', 3.960, 6.160, NULL),
  (41991, 158, 'But what if I told you it''s
not a character flaw but a mental habit?', 6.160, 10.460, NULL),
  (41992, 158, 'And if you watch
until the end of this video,', 10.460, 12.580, NULL),
  (41993, 158, 'I will show you how to break free
from it forever If we haven''t met,', 12.580, 17.200, NULL),
  (41994, 158, 'I''m Simon Alexander Ong, a coach, speaker', 17.280, 21.240, NULL),
  (41995, 158, 'and the bestselling author of Energize,
a book that''s helped thousands of people', 21.320, 25.680, NULL),
  (41996, 158, 'get unstuck and live with more energy,
clarity and confidence.', 25.860, 30.540, NULL),
  (41997, 158, 'And in the last decade,
I''ve had the privilege of working', 30.640, 33.820, NULL),
  (41998, 158, 'with everyone, from burned out executives', 33.820, 36.820, NULL),
  (41999, 158, 'to high performers struggling silently
with imposter syndrome.', 36.820, 40.960, NULL),
  (42000, 158, 'What I''m about to share isn''t theory.', 40.960, 43.020, NULL),
  (42001, 158, 'It''s the mindset shift that’s
helped people go from paralysis to power.', 43.020, 47.340, NULL),
  (42002, 158, 'One powerful shift simple yet effective', 47.340, 51.140, NULL),
  (42003, 158, 'that rewires
how you see yourself and silences', 51.220, 54.760, NULL),
  (42004, 158, 'the inner critic,
who''s been running your inner world,', 54.760, 57.420, NULL),
  (42005, 158, 'so that you may listen
to the guide within.', 57.420, 59.500, NULL),
  (42006, 158, 'And we will get there through story,
science and a powerful visual metaphor.', 59.500, 65.160, NULL),
  (42007, 158, 'Let''s first rewind to 1954,
where Roger Bannister', 65.160, 69.160, NULL),
  (42008, 158, 'does something the world believed
was physically impossible.', 69.160, 73.100, NULL),
  (42009, 158, 'He runs a mile in under 4 minutes.', 73.180, 76.140, NULL),
  (42010, 158, 'For years, experts had said the human body
simply couldn''t handle it:', 76.140, 80.680, NULL),
  (42011, 158, '“Too much drain.”
“The lungs would collapse.”', 80.760, 83.760, NULL),
  (42012, 158, '“The heart would fail.”
But here''s what''s truly mindblowing.', 83.820, 87.580, NULL),
  (42013, 158, 'Just 46 days later,
another runner broke the same record.', 87.580, 92.020, NULL),
  (42014, 158, 'And then dozens more followed.', 92.020, 93.680, NULL),
  (42015, 158, 'What changed?', 93.680, 94.540, NULL),
  (42016, 158, 'Not their bodies, but their beliefs.', 94.540, 96.980, NULL),
  (42017, 158, 'This is the invisible
prison of self-doubt.', 96.980, 100.200, NULL),
  (42018, 158, 'It doesn''t live in your abilities.', 100.200, 101.960, NULL),
  (42019, 158, 'It lives in your assumptions
about your abilities.', 101.960, 105.640, NULL),
  (42020, 158, 'You see, self-doubt
isn''t a sign that you''re not ready.', 105.640, 108.940, NULL),
  (42021, 158, 'It''s a sign that you haven''t updated
your inner operating system.', 108.940, 113.260, NULL),
  (42022, 158, 'You''re drawing conclusions from old data.', 113.260, 115.780, NULL),
  (42023, 158, 'What didn''t work when you were tired,
stressed, underprepared, or just younger.', 115.780, 120.540, NULL),
  (42024, 158, 'But now?', 120.680, 121.360, NULL),
  (42025, 158, 'You''re stronger, smarter, more resilient.', 121.360, 124.840, NULL),
  (42026, 158, 'And if you keep running today''s race
with yesterday''s mindset,', 124.920, 128.860, NULL),
  (42027, 158, 'you''ll always feel stuck.', 128.940, 130.660, NULL),
  (42028, 158, 'Let''s pause for a second and zoom out.', 130.660, 132.600, NULL),
  (42029, 158, 'The odds of you being born are 1 in
over 400 trillion.', 132.600, 136.840, NULL),
  (42030, 158, 'You are not here by accident.', 136.840, 138.780, NULL),
  (42031, 158, 'And self doubt dishonors
the miracle that you are.', 138.780, 141.840, NULL),
  (42032, 158, 'You''ve already won the greatest lottery
that there is going: the lottery of life.', 141.840, 146.900, NULL),
  (42033, 158, 'The question for you is this: “What
are you going to do with that winning', 146.900, 150.840, NULL),
  (42034, 158, 'ticket of yours?” Some people win
not because they''re better than you,', 150.840, 154.980, NULL),
  (42035, 158, 'but because they dare to believe harder
in the future version of themselves', 154.980, 158.900, NULL),
  (42036, 158, 'and their ability
to overcome the inevitable challenges', 158.980, 162.540, NULL),
  (42037, 158, 'and setbacks we all face
when journeying into the unknown.', 162.760, 166.420, NULL),
  (42038, 158, 'That''s not arrogance.', 166.420, 167.680, NULL),
  (42039, 158, 'That''s self leadership, courage and trust.', 167.680, 170.680, NULL),
  (42040, 158, 'A bird sitting on a tree
is never afraid of the branch breaking', 170.680, 174.820, NULL),
  (42041, 158, 'because its trust is not on the branch
but on its own wings.', 174.820, 178.640, NULL),
  (42042, 158, 'This is why it''s so important
to believe in yourself.', 178.640, 182.040, NULL),
  (42043, 158, 'And in case
no one has told you this recently.', 182.040, 184.240, NULL),
  (42044, 158, 'You are far stronger and more capable
than you think you are.', 184.240, 188.620, NULL),
  (42045, 158, 'Psychologists call this self-efficacy:
the belief in your ability to succeed.', 188.620, 193.560, NULL),
  (42046, 158, 'And one of the fastest ways to develop
this is through evidence stacking.', 193.560, 198.100, NULL),
  (42047, 158, 'Here''s how it works.', 198.100, 199.220, NULL),
  (42048, 158, 'Every time you follow through on a promise
to yourself,', 199.220, 202.640, NULL),
  (42049, 158, 'no matter how small,
you tell your brain, “I''m', 202.640, 205.720, NULL),
  (42050, 158, 'the kind of person who follows through.”
“I''m someone who gets things', 205.720, 210.140, NULL),
  (42051, 158, 'done.” “That voice
that told me I couldn''t?', 210.140, 213.340, NULL),
  (42052, 158, 'It lied.” And this is how you build
your new identity.', 213.420, 217.400, NULL),
  (42053, 158, 'One decision
and one moment of courage at a time.', 217.480, 221.340, NULL),
  (42054, 158, 'A coaching client of mine used to second
guess everything.', 221.340, 224.480, NULL),
  (42055, 158, 'New ideas? She''d overthink them.', 224.540, 226.720, NULL),
  (42056, 158, 'New opportunities?', 226.720, 228.040, NULL),
  (42057, 158, 'She''d say, “Who am I to do that?”
So we created a courage journal.', 228.040, 233.160, NULL),
  (42058, 158, 'One moment of brave action per day.', 233.300, 236.120, NULL),
  (42059, 158, 'That''s it.', 236.120, 236.720, NULL),
  (42060, 158, '30 days in, she looked back and told me
something I''ll never forget:', 236.720, 241.420, NULL),
  (42061, 158, '“I kept waiting for confidence
to show up before I acted.', 241.420, 246.460, NULL),
  (42062, 158, 'But now I know
confidence isn''t the starting line.', 246.540, 250.020, NULL),
  (42063, 158, 'It''s the finish line.”
Science tells us that by age 7, most of us', 250.020, 253.820, NULL),
  (42064, 158, 'have already formed core beliefs about
whether we''re lovable, capable or enough.', 253.820, 259.400, NULL),
  (42065, 158, 'We carry those beliefs with us
as we grow into adults.', 259.480, 262.480, NULL),
  (42066, 158, 'Beliefs that were written by moments
we barely remember.', 262.480, 265.320, NULL),
  (42067, 158, 'One sentence
from someone you looked up to.', 265.320, 267.540, NULL),
  (42068, 158, '“You''re not good enough”
or “You''ll never be successful.”', 267.540, 270.040, NULL),
  (42069, 158, 'And suddenly you spend decades
unconsciously proving them right.', 270.040, 273.840, NULL),
  (42070, 158, 'It''s not your fault. It''s your wiring.', 273.840, 276.720, NULL),
  (42071, 158, 'And the good news is
that wiring can be rewritten.', 276.720, 280.480, NULL),
  (42072, 158, 'Self-doubt doesn''t speak
just one language, though.', 280.480, 283.280, NULL),
  (42073, 158, 'It shows up in 4 ways.', 283.280, 285.260, NULL),
  (42074, 158, 'The first is overthinking
instead of acting.', 285.260, 288.380, NULL),
  (42075, 158, 'The second is hiding from visibility,
vulnerability or opportunity.', 288.380, 293.300, NULL),
