  (47954, 168, 'began by having
photovoltaic panels installed', 193.680, 196.560, NULL),
  (47955, 168, 'on all municipal
buildings.', 196.640, 198.360, NULL),
  (47956, 168, 'The generated electricity
was used for public lighting.', 198.440, 201.400, NULL),
  (47957, 168, 'In the process, Parris discovered
it saved the city a lot of money.', 201.440, 205.680, NULL),
  (47958, 168, 'The saved dollars were put
towards installing even more', 206.880, 209.760, NULL),
  (47959, 168, 'photovoltaic panels on the
roofs of private residences.', 209.760, 212.840, NULL),
  (47960, 168, 'These systems also became
mandatory for new buildings.', 212.840, 216.240, NULL),
  (47961, 168, 'Bit by bit, Lancaster created
an alternative energy network.', 216.760, 220.560, NULL),
  (47962, 168, 'Excess electricity started
being used to generate hydrogen', 221.240, 224.880, NULL),
  (47963, 168, 'to fuel public
transportation.', 225.000, 226.920, NULL),
  (47964, 168, 'The low-cost electricity and cheap
hydrogen', 227.000, 229.680, NULL),
  (47965, 168, 'attracted new, large companies.', 229.720, 231.720, NULL),
  (47966, 168, 'And Lancaster solidified its
reputation as a green boomtown', 231.800, 236.120, NULL),
  (47967, 168, 'in the United
States.', 236.120, 237.720, NULL),
  (47968, 168, 'I traveled a lot.', 237.800, 239.160, NULL),
  (47969, 168, 'I went to the World Economic Forum
in Tianjin, I went to Saudi Arabia,', 239.280, 244.000, NULL),
  (47970, 168, 'I went to the Middle East every energy
conference, and I learned a lot.', 244.000, 249.760, NULL),
  (47971, 168, 'Thanks to the
sunny weather', 253.680, 255.440, NULL),
  (47972, 168, 'and the already existing solar
and wind parks in the area,', 255.520, 258.880, NULL),
  (47973, 168, 'green energy and hydrogen
production continued to expand.', 258.880, 262.440, NULL),
  (47974, 168, 'When Lancaster began the process
of transforming its own energy system', 263.120, 267.280, NULL),
  (47975, 168, 'in 2009, the unemployment
rate was at 17%.', 267.280, 271.240, NULL),
  (47976, 168, 'In 2023, it dropped
to around 6%.', 271.240, 275.200, NULL),
  (47977, 168, 'Lancaster became a self-sufficient
green energy powerhouse', 275.680, 279.960, NULL),
  (47978, 168, 'and highly
profitable too.', 279.960, 281.640, NULL),
  (47979, 168, 'Once people start being
innovative and creative,', 281.720, 284.720, NULL),
  (47980, 168, 'it doesn’t stop with the
immediate goal in front of you.', 284.800, 287.160, NULL),
  (47981, 168, 'It extends
everywhere.', 287.160, 288.840, NULL),
  (47982, 168, 'This really is the most exciting city
in the world, I think,', 289.960, 293.560, NULL),
  (47983, 168, 'for that reason.', 293.640, 294.840, NULL),
  (47984, 168, 'We have a common purpose,
and it’s a simple purpose.', 294.920, 298.720, NULL),
  (47985, 168, 'It’s that our
children survive.', 298.720, 300.720, NULL),
  (47986, 168, 'You know, that’s
not hard, you know.', 300.800, 304.360, NULL),
  (47987, 168, 'And when you have that
as a common purpose,', 304.360, 307.160, NULL),
  (47988, 168, 'you can put aside all the differences
and you can make things happen.', 307.240, 311.600, NULL),
  (47989, 168, 'You can build things that
have never been built before.', 312.560, 315.560, NULL),
  (47990, 168, 'You know, this project here,
is actually quite remarkable.', 315.560, 319.200, NULL),
  (47991, 168, 'In recent years, both the city
of Lancaster and Mayor Parris', 322.600, 326.760, NULL),
  (47992, 168, 'have been recognized with
many awards for the achievement.', 326.760, 330.400, NULL),
  (47993, 168, 'From the US state of
California to Wunsiedel,', 331.360, 334.880, NULL),
  (47994, 168, 'in the German
state of Bavaria', 334.880, 336.800, NULL),
  (47995, 168, 'a rural region where
the forest industry is key.', 336.920, 339.920, NULL),
  (47996, 168, 'When Marco Krasser took the
helm of the regional energy supplier,', 342.880, 346.600, NULL),
  (47997, 168, 'everything
here changed.', 346.600, 348.720, NULL),
  (47998, 168, 'What would an
energy supply look like', 350.480, 352.440, NULL),
  (47999, 168, 'if we only could use renewable
energies', 352.440, 354.440, NULL),
  (48000, 168, 'and sustainable raw materials?', 354.480, 356.440, NULL),
  (48001, 168, 'Well, we harness sunlight
and wind energy and store them.', 356.440, 359.840, NULL),
  (48002, 168, 'Wunsiedel shifted
to a circular system', 360.880, 363.600, NULL),
  (48003, 168, 'that effectively linked its
regionally strong timber industry', 363.600, 367.440, NULL),
  (48004, 168, 'with the local
energy system.', 367.560, 369.400, NULL),
  (48005, 168, 'The idea was to re-use as much
energy as possible, multiple times.', 369.880, 374.960, NULL),
  (48006, 168, 'And wherever excess
energy accumulated', 374.960, 377.440, NULL),
  (48007, 168, 'say, in the form of wood waste
or waste-heat from machines', 377.520, 381.160, NULL),
  (48008, 168, 'it shouldn’t be lost
but rather harnessed.', 381.240, 383.960, NULL),
  (48009, 168, 'We have wood, we have
biomass, we have sun and wind.', 391.240, 394.480, NULL),
  (48010, 168, 'We may not have hydropower, but we
use everything locally that we need.', 394.600, 398.640, NULL),
  (48011, 168, 'Surplus energy generated
from solar and wind power', 402.080, 405.400, NULL),
  (48012, 168, 'is used to press forestry
waste into wood pellets.', 405.400, 408.520, NULL),
  (48013, 168, 'The pellets can then be
burned to generate heat,', 411.040, 413.800, NULL),
  (48014, 168, 'or to power a
turbine for electricity.', 413.800, 416.280, NULL),
  (48015, 168, 'It forms a cascaded system which
always consists of the same thing:', 420.960, 424.640, NULL),
  (48016, 168, 'solar and wind, battery storage,
and combined heat and power.', 424.640, 428.480, NULL),
  (48017, 168, 'It’s the perfect system which
couples both sectors and industries.', 428.920, 432.400, NULL),
  (48018, 168, 'The construction industry is
linked to the timber industry;', 432.400, 435.480, NULL),
  (48019, 168, 'the timber industry is linked
with agriculture or forestry.', 435.480, 439.200, NULL),
  (48020, 168, 'This creates local circular energy
economies that can be scaled up', 441.240, 444.240, NULL),
  (48021, 168, 'to all levels, which in turn
satisfy the energy demand', 444.240, 447.920, NULL),
  (48022, 168, 'in the form of
electricity and heat.', 447.920, 450.240, NULL),
  (48023, 168, 'And electricity in
terms of mobility.', 450.320, 452.720, NULL),
  (48024, 168, 'Wunsiedel in Bavaria
and Lancaster in California:', 461.200, 465.760, NULL),
  (48025, 168, 'Both have tapped into their locally
available resources as best they can.', 465.760, 470.360, NULL),
  (48026, 168, 'And both have created
infrastructures in which green energy', 470.440, 474.160, NULL),
  (48027, 168, 'can be used as efficiently as
possible in an ongoing cycle.', 474.240, 477.960, NULL),
  (48028, 168, 'Of course, such systems
are ideally integrated', 481.640, 484.520, NULL),
  (48029, 168, 'into construction projects
from the very start.', 484.600, 487.520, NULL),
  (48030, 168, 'In Copenhagen, a newly-built
district called Nordhavn', 489.520, 493.360, NULL),
  (48031, 168, 'served as the testing ground
for the “EnergyLab” project', 493.360, 496.480, NULL),
  (48032, 168, 'a living laboratory for
research into innovative', 496.880, 499.880, NULL),
  (48033, 168, 'and more efficient
energy cycles.', 499.960, 502.120, NULL),
  (48034, 168, 'Well, the essence is that we
test the solutions in real life.', 508.680, 512.520, NULL),
  (48035, 168, 'In EnergyLab Nordhavn, we have
also been looking into business models', 512.560, 516.560, NULL),
  (48036, 168, 'because that’s also
part of the solution.', 518.000, 520.280, NULL),
  (48037, 168, 'Innovation and business
models is part of the solution.', 520.280, 523.760, NULL),
  (48038, 168, 'In this sector coupling context,
it’s very important that we utilize', 523.840, 527.360, NULL),
  (48039, 168, 'the energy that is available
and this is basically something', 527.360, 530.400, NULL),
  (48040, 168, 'that we are demonstrating
here in the Nordhavn project.', 530.400, 533.200, NULL),
  (48041, 168, 'We can say that the energy
system has to develop,', 533.200, 536.280, NULL),
  (48042, 168, 'we have to do it in
a more smart way,', 536.360, 538.320, NULL),
  (48043, 168, 'and that means that we need to
see what other sources are available', 538.320, 542.520, NULL),
  (48044, 168, 'and how can we in the best
possible way actually utilize them.', 542.600, 545.600, NULL),
  (48045, 168, 'The buildings here are
well-insulated and retain heat.', 545.600, 549.840, NULL),
  (48046, 168, 'That’s a money-saver — and is
especially important at peak hours', 549.840, 553.840, NULL),
  (48047, 168, 'in the early
mornings.', 553.960, 555.640, NULL),
  (48048, 168, 'Plus, commercial businesses
in the neighborhood', 555.720, 558.320, NULL),
  (48049, 168, 'can compress
their waste-heat', 558.320, 559.880, NULL),
  (48050, 168, 'and supply it to the
district heating system,', 559.880, 562.640, NULL),
  (48051, 168, 'which provides heat to
the surrounding buildings.', 562.640, 565.680, NULL),
  (48052, 168, 'The compressors for
cooling down the goods,', 565.760, 568.560, NULL),
  (48053, 168, 'they are run by electricity and
by using a little bit more electricity', 568.640, 572.440, NULL),
  (48054, 168, 'in the compressors, we
get way more heat available.', 572.440, 575.320, NULL),
  (48055, 168, 'So in situations where we have
surplus electricity from wind turbines', 575.320, 579.280, NULL),
  (48056, 168, 'or photovoltaic, we can
actually optimize operation', 579.280, 583.360, NULL),
  (48057, 168, 'of the compressors and
convert that into a lot extra energy', 583.360, 587.080, NULL),
  (48058, 168, 'that can be used
in the buildings.', 587.160, 588.880, NULL),
  (48059, 168, 'And in that way, is this system
actually a smart component', 588.880, 592.520, NULL),
  (48060, 168, 'in the sector coupled
energy system.', 592.640, 594.960, NULL),
  (48061, 168, 'Here again, an ingenious cycle.', 595.040, 597.120, NULL),
  (48062, 168, 'The energy put into the system', 597.160, 598.960, NULL),
  (48063, 168, 'is not single-purpose —
rather, it’s used several times.', 599.040, 601.880, NULL),
  (48064, 168, 'And the whole
neighborhood benefits.', 601.880, 604.200, NULL),
  (48065, 168, 'The goal of a modern circular
economy is to save energy', 625.640, 629.640, NULL),
  (48066, 168, 'and increase
efficiency.', 629.640, 631.920, NULL),
  (48067, 168, 'These cycles are optimized to
make energy competitive in price', 631.920, 635.840, NULL),
  (48068, 168, 'while serving as an extension
or even an alternative to the large,', 635.920, 640.080, NULL),
  (48069, 168, 'centralized grids.', 640.160, 641.600, NULL),
  (48070, 168, 'Norway and its capital
Oslo are among the pioneers', 651.720, 655.440, NULL),
  (48071, 168, 'in the green
energy transition.', 655.440, 657.440, NULL),
  (48072, 168, 'Oslo is aiming to reduce
CO2 emissions to zero by 2030.', 658.080, 663.080, NULL),
  (48073, 168, 'Mayor Marianne Borgen', 669.920, 671.840, NULL),
  (48074, 168, 'helped to draft and pass a
series of concrete measures.', 671.880, 674.800, NULL),
  (48075, 168, 'We have all the way
tried to tell our inhabitants', 676.920, 681.240, NULL),
  (48076, 168, 'that this is not
about restrictions.', 681.920, 684.240, NULL),
  (48077, 168, 'So it’s not about
restrictions.', 684.320, 686.320, NULL),
  (48078, 168, 'It''s about
opportunities.', 686.400, 689.200, NULL),
  (48079, 168, 'When we are building new
kindergartens and schools,', 689.920, 693.120, NULL),
  (48080, 168, 'they are built with
solar cell panels.', 693.720, 696.200, NULL),
  (48081, 168, 'And they also produce more energy
than they need to use themselves.', 696.280, 700.480, NULL),
  (48082, 168, 'So we can put it over
to other buildings nearby.', 703.280, 706.280, NULL),
  (48083, 168, 'Oslo is considered the
world capital of e-mobility.', 709.080, 713.000, NULL),
  (48084, 168, 'It’s also made
significant headway', 713.000, 715.200, NULL),
  (48085, 168, 'in making its construction sector
carbon-neutral with advancements', 715.280, 719.440, NULL),
  (48086, 168, 'in heating and
building materials.', 719.520, 720.920, NULL),
  (48087, 168, 'We have said in Oslo that we want
to be the first zero emission city', 724.400, 730.160, NULL),
  (48088, 168, 'in the world by 2030, which is a very
ambitious goal, but it is possible.', 730.160, 736.120, NULL),
  (48089, 168, 'I think that is so important both
to try to reduce the consumption,', 736.120, 741.000, NULL),
  (48090, 168, 'of course, but also reduce the waste
and also to reuse and also recycle.', 741.000, 748.120, NULL),
  (48091, 168, 'I think that these are all important
elements in the total policy.', 748.120, 752.280, NULL),
  (48092, 168, 'To achieve this
ambitious goal,', 754.680, 757.160, NULL),
  (48093, 168, 'both residents and businesses
must play an active part.', 757.160, 760.600, NULL),
  (48094, 168, 'Hege Schøyen Dillner spent
several years of her career working', 762.320, 766.240, NULL),
  (48095, 168, 'at a large Scandinavian
construction company based in Oslo.', 766.320, 770.000, NULL),
  (48096, 168, 'The company has more
than 8,000 employees', 770.560, 773.200, NULL),
  (48097, 168, 'and carries out
projects worldwide.', 773.280, 775.560, NULL),
  (48098, 168, 'As a board member, she pushed
the company to publicly commit', 775.640, 779.400, NULL),
  (48099, 168, 'to implementing the goals of the 2015
Paris Agreement on climate change.', 779.520, 783.520, NULL),
  (48100, 168, 'She also supported
Mayor Borgen''s measures.', 783.520, 786.320, NULL),
  (48101, 168, 'I think the biggest
moment in my career', 787.760, 791.320, NULL),
  (48102, 168, 'was when the whole
management team', 791.320, 794.000, NULL),
  (48103, 168, 'decided that we would work
towards the Paris Agreement.', 794.000, 800.640, NULL),
  (48104, 168, 'We didn’t know exactly how we should
do it, but we set a clear direction.', 800.640, 806.760, NULL),
  (48105, 168, 'And I think that was so
crucial, to set the direction.', 806.760, 810.160, NULL),
  (48106, 168, 'And then some people said:
But what if we can’t make it?', 810.240, 813.760, NULL),
  (48107, 168, 'And I said: Well, I’m
not so afraid about that.', 813.840, 818.120, NULL),
  (48108, 168, 'I''m afraid that we don''t
dare to set the direction.', 820.520, 823.720, NULL),
  (48109, 168, 'With all her experience, Hege
Schøyen Dillner sat for years', 825.520, 829.200, NULL),
  (48110, 168, 'on the board of the Norwegian
Green Building Council,', 829.280, 832.080, NULL),
  (48111, 168, 'which is part of the World
Green Building Council.', 832.080, 835.200, NULL),
  (48112, 168, 'I think it will be very important how
we build our cities the next 30 years.', 836.440, 842.840, NULL),
  (48113, 168, 'In 2022, we reached eight
billion people on Earth,', 843.640, 848.880, NULL),
  (48114, 168, 'and by 2050 there
will be 10 billions.', 848.880, 853.120, NULL),
  (48115, 168, 'That means a city the size of Vienna
will be built every week until 2050.', 853.120, 860.680, NULL),
  (48116, 168, 'That''s a lot of aluminum and steel
and glass and wood and concrete', 860.680, 865.640, NULL),
  (48117, 168, 'and plastic
and bricks.', 865.640, 868.640, NULL),
  (48118, 168, 'So we have
to go circular.', 868.640, 871.640, NULL),
  (48119, 168, 'We have to build
with less for longer.', 871.640, 877.200, NULL),
  (48120, 168, 'Sonja Horn manages a real
estate company in Norway.', 881.000, 884.680, NULL),
  (48121, 168, 'When constructing
new buildings,', 884.680, 886.560, NULL),
  (48122, 168, 'the company aims to reuse as many
elements as possible from old office', 886.560, 890.960, NULL),
  (48123, 168, 'buildings that are
being torn down.', 891.040, 892.840, NULL),
  (48124, 168, 'When building a modern office complex
in Oslo,', 895.960, 898.840, NULL),
  (48125, 168, 'the company fused old with new.', 898.920, 901.400, NULL),
  (48126, 168, 'It was a pilot project, meaning
success was not guaranteed.', 901.400, 905.080, NULL),
  (48127, 168, 'But almost immediately, startups
and tenants started moving in', 905.160, 909.080, NULL),
  (48128, 168, 'precisely because they
were drawn to the concept.', 909.160, 912.240, NULL),
  (48129, 168, 'Hege Schøyen Dillner also
had an office there for some time.', 912.320, 916.080, NULL),
  (48130, 168, 'It’s a reused
reflector panel.', 917.480, 920.640, NULL),
  (48131, 168, 'Also the fence here used to be
on the floor in the swimming pool', 920.640, 925.440, NULL),
  (48132, 168, 'in the technical room and
is being used all the way', 925.440, 929.120, NULL),
  (48133, 168, 'up as a railing
in the atrium.', 929.280, 931.240, NULL),
  (48134, 168, 'So those are some of the
more interior aspects of re-use,', 932.240, 935.840, NULL),
  (48135, 168, 'we also refer to
it as upcycling.', 935.960, 938.080, NULL),
  (48136, 168, 'So it goes from one thing to
be upcycled to something else.', 938.160, 941.880, NULL),
  (48137, 168, 'We’ve been working
systematically on finding out', 941.960, 946.160, NULL),
  (48138, 168, 'how we can make
buildings part of the solution.', 946.160, 950.680, NULL),
  (48139, 168, 'I mean, buildings account for around
40% of carbon emissions globally,', 950.680, 957.120, NULL),
  (48140, 168, '40% of energy use, so a
huge part of the problem.', 957.120, 960.640, NULL),
  (48141, 168, 'Meaning that we also
have the opportunity', 960.640, 963.320, NULL),
  (48142, 168, 'to be a huge part
of the solution.', 963.400, 965.600, NULL),
  (48143, 168, 'In 2019, an
office building', 970.880, 973.360, NULL),
  (48144, 168, 'commissioned by Sonja
Horn''s company was inaugurated', 973.360, 976.600, NULL),
  (48145, 168, 'in the Norwegian
city of Trondheim.', 976.680, 978.280, NULL),
  (48146, 168, 'It was named:
"Powerhouse."', 978.280, 980.960, NULL),
  (48147, 168, 'The roof is covered
with solar panels,', 980.960, 983.400, NULL),
  (48148, 168, 'angled optimally to capture
the sun’s rays in northern Europe.', 983.520, 987.160, NULL),
  (48149, 168, 'As a result, the Powerhouse, with
its 3,000 square meters of panels,', 987.160, 992.320, NULL),
  (48150, 168, 'produces an annual average of
500,000 kilowatt hours of electricity.', 992.320, 997.720, NULL),
  (48151, 168, 'That is more than double
the amount it consumes itself.', 997.720, 1001.160, NULL),
  (48152, 168, 'The surplus electricity is
used on a local micro-grid', 1001.240, 1004.560, NULL),
  (48153, 168, 'to supply neighboring buildings,
and electric buses and cars.', 1004.640, 1008.480, NULL),
  (48154, 168, 'And this is a pioneer project, it’s
one of a kind, the first of its kind.', 1012.360, 1017.280, NULL),
  (48155, 168, 'So it’s attractive for young
people to sit and work here.', 1017.280, 1021.680, NULL),
  (48156, 168, 'And it feels good.', 1021.680, 1025.520, NULL),
  (48157, 168, 'Whenever we build new, we have
focused on mainly three aspects:', 1025.520, 1029.480, NULL),
  (48158, 168, 'One is to use less
resources and materials,', 1030.080, 1032.880, NULL),
  (48159, 168, 'so whatever you
can reuse is excellent.', 1034.440, 1036.960, NULL),
  (48160, 168, 'If you can’t reuse, maybe
you can use recycled materials', 1037.880, 1042.320, NULL),
  (48161, 168, 'before you start
sourcing new materials.', 1042.320, 1044.920, NULL),
  (48162, 168, 'More and more of the construction
sites that we have in Oslo', 1045.040, 1049.600, NULL),
  (48163, 168, 'are now zero emission
construction site', 1049.600, 1051.680, NULL),
  (48164, 168, 'because the
technology is in place.', 1051.680, 1053.640, NULL),
  (48165, 168, 'We need to challenge
the establishments,', 1053.640, 1057.160, NULL),
  (48166, 168, 'the industry and also show the way.', 1057.160, 1060.000, NULL),
  (48167, 168, 'The employers and employees', 1060.000, 1061.680, NULL),
  (48168, 168, 'in business
are now largely as a general trend,', 1061.720, 1065.240, NULL),
  (48169, 168, 'very much on board,
that cutting emissions', 1065.240, 1068.560, NULL),
  (48170, 168, 'is not only the right thing
to do for the world''s climate', 1068.560, 1072.160, NULL),
  (48171, 168, 'and the future of our kids but is
actually also smart in the economy.', 1072.240, 1075.320, NULL),
  (48172, 168, 'Like Oslo, the rest of Norway is
aiming to be carbon neutral by 2030.', 1075.600, 1080.880, NULL),
  (48173, 168, 'The country has a
large oil and gas sector,', 1081.560, 1084.360, NULL),
  (48174, 168, 'but it also has a
wealth of hydropower.', 1084.480, 1087.000, NULL),
  (48175, 168, 'Norwegian Minister Espen
Barth Eide is confident', 1089.200, 1092.000, NULL),
  (48176, 168, 'that the necessary transition
to a carbon-neutral economy', 1092.000, 1095.600, NULL),
  (48177, 168, 'comes with more opportunities
than risks for domestic industries.', 1095.680, 1099.760, NULL),
  (48178, 168, 'We’re also seeing that the
service industry that was developed', 1101.040, 1104.920, NULL),
  (48179, 168, 'because of the 50
years of petroleum', 1105.000, 1107.360, NULL),
  (48180, 168, 'is now very eager to themselves
go into these new areas.', 1107.440, 1111.600, NULL),
  (48181, 168, 'Because if you can run oil or
gas platforms in the North Sea', 1111.600, 1115.360, NULL),
  (48182, 168, 'in 10-meter high waves
and extreme conditions,', 1115.480, 1117.640, NULL),
  (48183, 168, 'you can also
do floating wind.', 1117.640, 1119.200, NULL),
  (48184, 168, 'If you’re good at building fossil
ships with advanced technology,', 1119.200, 1122.720, NULL),
  (48185, 168, 'you’re also good at building
hydrogen or ammonia driven ships', 1122.720, 1125.640, NULL),
  (48186, 168, 'with advanced
technology.', 1125.640, 1127.320, NULL),
  (48187, 168, 'This circular energy economy relies
as much on technological innovation', 1128.520, 1133.000, NULL),
  (48188, 168, 'from major industries
as it does on a stable grid', 1133.080, 1136.160, NULL),
  (48189, 168, 'that can provide constant
and reliable green power.', 1136.240, 1139.880, NULL),
  (48190, 168, 'In northern Europe, that can
best be achieved with wind power', 1140.120, 1143.960, NULL),
